  "goodToKnow": "Die Belagerung is a siege: die Belagerung Wiens (1683, by the Ottomans), die Belagerung Leningrads (1941–1944, by the German Wehrmacht, about a million civilians died). The verb belagern means to besiege, and colloquially to crowd around: Fans belagerten das Hotel. It comes from das Lager (camp), the camp set up around a city. Plural: die Belagerungen."
